{
  "id": "notepad_plus_plus",
  "name": "Notepad++",
  "kind": "app",
  "category": "Development",
  "match": {
    "windows_exe": [
      "notepad++.exe"
    ],
    "window_title": []
  },
  "sources": [
    "https://npp-user-manual.org/docs/editing/",
    "https://npp-user-manual.org/docs/preferences/#shortcut-mapper",
    "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/notepad-plus-plus/npp-usermanual/master/content/docs/editing.md",
    "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/notepad-plus-plus/notepad-plus-plus/master/PowerEditor/src/Parameters.cpp",
    "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/notepad-plus-plus/notepad-plus-plus/master/PowerEditor/src/Notepad_plus.rc"
  ],
  "note": "Windows only. The Notepad++ User Manual describes the Shortcut Mapper but does not print the Main menu tab's default assignments, so this file combines the two places Notepad++ does publish them. The editor commands are the manual's own \"Scintilla SCI_xxx Keyboard Commands\" table on the Editing page, with its Default Shortcut column; their names are the SCI_ message names, which is exactly what the Shortcut Mapper's \"Scintilla commands\" tab shows (\"The Name matches the menu item, or the name of the Scintilla message\"). The menu commands come from Notepad++'s own default accelerator table, winKeyDefs[] in PowerEditor/src/Parameters.cpp, with the command names taken from the menu labels in PowerEditor/src/Notepad_plus.rc (ampersand accelerators removed) or from the cmdName the table itself gives. Manual prose was not used as a source for individual bindings: it contains at least one error (the Files page gives Ctrl+N as the shortcut for File > Open). Commands the tables list without a default shortcut are left out, as are the numeric-keypad bindings for Ctrl+Keypad 0-9 (fold level) and the SCI_ commands the manual marks as not being in the Shortcut Mapper. Where a command has two default accelerators the letter or digit one is kept (Cut is Ctrl+X, not Shift+Delete); where the manual lists two shortcuts for one SCI_ command the first is kept. These are the factory defaults - the Shortcut Mapper can change any of them.",
